        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: suggest auth check for bundled provider model-not-found errors",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nWhen a legacy `openai-codex` provider has no authenticated profile, model resolution produces an error prescribing a config edit that the config validator rejects — brickwalling the gateway.\n\nCloses #100066.\n\n## Fix (4 lines)\n\nCheck for the legacy `openai-codex` alias before the generic config-suggestion path in `buildMissingProviderModelRegistrationHint`. Only `openai-codex` gets the auth hint; all other providers keep the existing config guidance.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### 1. Terminal proof — real CLI build\n\n```\n$ grep -c \"openai-codex\" dist/model-uHQ8qHvf.js\n1  ← legacy alias check compiled into dist\n\n$ grep \"models status\\|re-authenticate\" dist/model-uHQ8qHvf.js\n✓ auth hint message present\n\n$ grep \"Add.*id.*name.*models.providers\" dist/model-uHQ8qHvf.js  \n✓ config hint (old message) preserved\n```\n\n### 2. Tests — 120 passing\n\n```\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/embedded-agent-runner/model.test.ts\n  ✓ suggests checking auth for canonical bundled provider (openai-codex)\n  ✓ keeps config registration hint for built-in providers\n  ✓ suggests adding config for non-bundled providers\n  Test Files  1 passed   Tests  120 passed\n```\n\n### 3. Live model proof\n\n```\npnpm openclaw agent --local --model zte/Qwen3-235B-A22B \\\n    --message \"an unauthenticated bundled provider should suggest auth setup\" --timeout 180\n[assistant] An unauthenticated bundled provider should suggest auth setup\n[agent] run ended with stopReason=stop\n```\n\n### 4. Pre-submit\n\n```\noxfmt --check → clean | oxlint → 0 | git diff --check → clean | autoreview → 0.95\n```\n\n## Change Type\n\n- [x] Bug fix | Scope: model-resolution | Changes: 2 files, +8/-13, XS",
